---
// Verbatim Authentic Content & Media from Khao Sok Riverside Cottages
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

---

<PageLayout
  title="Khao Sok Jungle Wildlife and Plants"
  description="Explore Khao Sok wildlife, including mammals, birds, reptiles and rainforest plants. Find the best tours for wildlife viewing."
  heroImage="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/khao-national-park-elephant.jpg"
  heroTitle="Khao Sok Jungle Wildlife and Plants"
  heroSubtitle="The Ancient Rainforest of Southern Thailand"
  breadcrumbs={[{"label": "Khao Sok Jungle Thailand Rai...", "href": "/khao-sok-jungle-thailand-rainforest/"}]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10">
    <div class="bg-[#faf8f5]/95 border border-[#12281b]/10 rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-8 md:p-12 shadow-2xl backdrop-blur-md">
      
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#12281b]/10 pb-4 mb-8 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-[#163824]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold">
          <span class="text-[#7a5813]">KSR</span>
          <span class="text-[#12281b]/20">/</span>
          <span>FIELD DISPATCH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="text-[#7a5813] font-bold">KHAO SOK · THAILAND</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[#223e2c] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Khao Sok Wildlife Guide</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          This Khao Sok Wildlife Guide explores one of the oldest rainforests in the world and the extraordinary variety of animals and plants found in Khao Sok National Park. Visitors may encounter gibbons, hornbills, macaques and monitor lizards, while more elusive species such as tapirs, pangolins and sun bears remain rare and memorable sightings.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          This guide highlights some of the animals and plants found in Khao Sok, along with the activities that offer the best opportunities to see them. Start by exploring a wildlife category, or browse 'Best Activities for Viewing Wildlife' to discover which experiences offer the greatest chance of memorable wildlife encounters.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          For an overview of the area, please have a look at our <a href="/khao-sok-national-park/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Khao Sok National Park</a> page
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Explore by Category</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#mammals">&#x1f418; Mammals →</a><br /> <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#reptiles">&#x1f98e; Reptiles & Amphibians →</a><br /> <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#birds">&#x1f426; Birds →</a><br /> <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#insects">&#x1f577;&#xfe0f; Insects & Arachnids →</a><br /> <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#plants">&#x1f33f; Rainforest Plants →</a><br /> <a class="fusion-one-page-text-link guide-link" href="#fungi">&#x1f344; Fungi →</a>
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>BEST ACTIVITIES FOR VIEWING WILDLIFE</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Riverside Cottages.</strong> Wildlife abounds at Riverside Cottages. Regular sightings include Macaques, Monitor Lizards, Kingfishers, Owls and Flying Dragons. Occasional visitors include Slow Loris, Otters and Hornbills.
        </p>
        <div class="my-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/70 shadow-md">
          <table width="100%"><thead><tr><th style="color: #000000; font-size: 22px;" align="left">Activity</th><th style="color: #000000; font-size: 22px;" align="left">Wildlife Highlights</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Lake Tours</td><td align="left">Gibbon, Langur, Hornbill, Crested Serpent Eagle, Tapir*, Gaur*, Elephant*</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Jungle Hike</td><td align="left">Langur, Macaque, Pitta, Kingfisher, Reptiles & Rainforest Plants</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Bang Man Hike</td><td align="left">Hornbill, Gibbon, Crested Serpent Eagle</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Canoe Trip</td><td align="left">Otter, Kingfisher, Monitor Lizard, Macaque, Mangrove Cat Snakes, Reticulated Python</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Night Safari</td><td align="left">Slow Loris, Brown Wood Owl, Tokay Gecko, Tree Frog, Reticulated Python, Mangrove Cat Snake</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Overnight Camping</td><td align="left">Slow Loris, Hornbill, Pangolin*, Tapir*, Sun Bear*</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Birdwatching</td><td align="left">Hornbill, Pitta, Kingfisher, Crested Serpent Eagle, Brown Wood Owl</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Elephant Sanctuary</td><td align="left">Elephant</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Rafflesia Trek</td><td align="left">Rafflesia (when flowering), Pitcher Plant, Rainforest Plants</td></tr></tbody></table>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          *Rare wildlife sightings. Never guaranteed.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>MAMMALS</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is home to an impressive variety of mammals. Visitors may encounter playful otters, curious macaques, elusive tapirs, sun bears and even wild elephants.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Some species are seen regularly. Others are rarely encountered. That sense of unpredictability makes every wildlife sighting a memorable part of the rainforest experience.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The rainforest also supports several exceptionally elusive species, including mouse deer, binturongs and, historically, tigers.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These animals remain part of Khao Sok's rich biodiversity. However, most visitors will never encounter them in the wild.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Asian Elephant</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Asian elephants are among the most iconic animals found in Khao Sok National Park. Wild elephants still roam parts of the rainforest and surrounding protected areas. However, sightings are relatively uncommon and should be considered a fortunate wildlife encounter rather than an expectation.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These intelligent and highly social animals live in family groups led by an experienced female matriarch. They spend much of their day feeding on grasses, leaves, fruits and other vegetation. Visitors are most likely to encounter signs of elephant activity during overnight lake trips and longer jungle excursions.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          To learn more about these remarkable animals, <a href="/khao-sok-elephant-sanctuary/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">visit an ethical Elephant Sanctuary</a> or read our detailed guide to the <a href="/asian-elephant-khao-sok-national-park-elephant/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Asian Elephant in Khao Sok National Park</a>.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/khao-national-park-elephant.jpg"
            alt="Khao national park elephant"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Khao national park elephant</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities:</strong> <a href="/khao-sok-lake-cheow-lan-tours/#overnightcheowlan" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Lake Tours</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-thailand-adventures/#elephants" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Elephant Sanctuary</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>White-handed Gibbon</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The White-handed Gibbon is one of the most sought-after wildlife sightings in Khao Sok National Park. These agile apes spend most of their lives high in the rainforest canopy and are not always easy to spot. However, visitors often hear their distinctive calls echoing through the jungle during the early morning.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Unlike monkeys, gibbons belong to the ape family and do not have tails. Their long arms allow them to swing effortlessly through the treetops. They can cover remarkable distances as they move between trees.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          White-handed Gibbons are more often heard than seen. Their haunting calls are one of the most memorable sounds of the Khao Sok rainforest. Sightings are never guaranteed, but hearing a gibbon call is a highlight of many visits.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/gibbons-thailand.jpg"
            alt="Thailand Gibbons"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Thailand Gibbons</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities</strong>: <a href="/khao-sok-lake-cheow-lan-tours/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Lake Tours</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Jungle Hike</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Bang Man Hike</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Spectacled Langur</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Spectacled Langur is one of the primates most commonly seen in Khao Sok National Park. Also known as the Dusky Leaf Monkey, it is easily recognised by the distinctive white rings around its eyes and mouth, which resemble a pair of spectacles.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Living high in the forest canopy, these gentle monkeys feed mainly on leaves, fruits, seeds and flowers. Visitors often spot them in the early morning or late afternoon, resting in the treetops or moving quietly through the jungle.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Perhaps the most remarkable feature of the Spectacled Langur is its bright orange newborns. These striking infants gradually change colour during their first few months of life before developing the grey coat of an adult langur.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/spectacled-lemur-leaf-monkey-2.jpg"
            alt="Spectacled Langur - Khao Sok jungle"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Spectacled Langur - Khao Sok jungle</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities:</strong> <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Jungle Hike</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-lake-cheow-lan-tours/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Lake Tours</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-thailand-adventures/#camping" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Jungle Camping</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Long-tailed Macaque</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Long-tailed Macaque is the monkey visitors are most likely to encounter in Khao Sok National Park. Troops of these curious and highly adaptable primates are often seen around <a href="/khao-sok-riverside-resort-facilities/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Riverside Cottages</a>. They can frequently be observed from Rafflesia Café as they move through the trees along the riverbank.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Living in social groups, macaques spend much of their day feeding, grooming and interacting with one another. Their varied diet includes fruits, seeds, leaves, insects and other small animals. This adaptability allows them to thrive in a wide range of habitats throughout the rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although accustomed to people, macaques are still wild animals. They should never be fed or approached too closely.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/macaque-monkey-thailand.jpg"
            alt="Macaque monkey - Thailand rainforest"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Macaque monkey - Thailand rainforest</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities:</strong> Riverside Cottages | <a href="/khao-sok-restaurant/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Rafflesia Café</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-thailand-adventures/#canoetrip" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Canoe Trip</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Jungle Hikes</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-lake-cheow-lan-tours/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Lake Tours</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Slow Loris</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Slow Loris is one of the most unusual mammals found in the Khao Sok rainforest. These small nocturnal primates spend their days sleeping in dense vegetation. After dark, they become active and move slowly through the trees in search of insects, fruit and tree sap.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite their gentle appearance, Slow Lorises have an extraordinary adaptation. They are one of the few venomous mammals in the world. A toxin produced near their elbows helps protect them from predators.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Because they are active at night, Slow Lorises can be difficult to spot. They also spend much of their time hidden in the forest canopy. Sightings are never guaranteed. However, lucky visitors occasionally encounter Slow Lorises during night safaris or around Riverside Cottages after dark.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/slow-loris-khao-sok.jpg"
            alt="Slow Loris"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Slow Loris</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities:</strong> <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/#night" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Night Safari</a> | Riverside Cottages
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Asian Small-clawed Otter</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Asian Small-clawed Otter is the smallest otter species in the world and one of the most charming mammals found in Khao Sok. Highly social and intelligent, these playful animals live in family groups. They spend much of their time searching for fish, crabs, insects and other small prey along rivers and streams.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although sightings are never guaranteed, lucky visitors occasionally spot otters swimming, feeding or playing along the Sok River. Their curious nature and energetic behaviour make them one of the most rewarding wildlife encounters in the rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Otters are most active during the cooler hours of the day. Early morning and late afternoon generally offer the best chance of a sighting.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/asian-small-clawed-otter.jpg"
            alt="Asian Small-clawed Otter"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Asian Small-clawed Otter</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities:</strong> Riverside Cottages | <a href="/khao-sok-thailand-adventures/#canoetrip" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Canoe Trip</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-lake-cheow-lan-tours/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Lake Tours</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Malayan Tapir</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Malayan Tapir is one of the most distinctive and elusive mammals found in Khao Sok National Park. Recognisable by its striking black-and-white colouring and unusual shape, the tapir is often described as looking like a cross between a pig and an elephant. Despite its size, it is a shy and secretive animal that spends much of its time hidden deep within the rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Tapirs are strongly associated with rivers, streams and wetlands. Excellent swimmers, they can even walk along the bottom of a river while using their flexible snout as a snorkel. They are most active during the evening and at night, emerging from the forest to feed on leaves, shoots and fruit.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Sightings of Malayan Tapirs in Khao Sok are extremely rare and should be considered a truly special wildlife encounter. However, visitors exploring more remote areas of the rainforest may occasionally encounter signs of their presence.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/tapir-khao-sok-jungle.jpg"
            alt="Khao Sok jungle Tapir"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Khao Sok jungle Tapir</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Best Viewing Opportunities: <a href="/khao-sok-lake-cheow-lan-tours/#overnightcheowlan" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Lake Tours</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Gaur</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Gaur is the largest wild cattle species in the world and one of the most impressive animals found in Khao Sok National Park. These powerful herbivores can weigh more than a tonne. They are easily recognised by their thick curved horns and distinctive white lower legs, which give them the appearance of wearing socks.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Gaurs live in small family groups and spend much of their time feeding on grasses, leaves and other vegetation in remote forest areas. Despite their size, they are often surprisingly difficult to spot in the dense rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although sightings are uncommon, Gaur are occasionally seen around Cheow Lan Lake. The more open landscape offers visitors the best chance of encountering them.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/khao-sok-wildlife.jpg"
            alt="Gaur - Thailand rainforest"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
