        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Pangolin</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Pangolin is one of the most remarkable mammals found in the Khao Sok rainforest. Covered in protective scales made from keratin, it is the only mammal in the world with this unique armour.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Pangolins are nocturnal and spend much of their time searching for ants and termites. Their powerful claws allow them to break open nests, while their long sticky tongue is perfectly adapted for feeding on insects hidden deep inside.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite being one of Khao Sok's most iconic animals, Pangolins are exceptionally difficult to find in the wild. Most visitors will never encounter one, making any sighting a truly special wildlife experience.
        </p>
