        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>REPTILES & AMPHIBIANS</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Khao Sok rainforest is home to a fascinating variety of reptiles and amphibians. These include colourful tree frogs and geckos, as well as monitor lizards, flying dragons and snakes.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Many of these animals are most active during the cooler hours of the day or after dark. This makes them a highlight of night walks and wildlife-focused adventures.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although some snake species found in Thailand are venomous, encounters are uncommon. Serious incidents involving visitors are extremely rare. As with all wildlife, reptiles should be observed from a respectful distance and never disturbed.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Asian Water Monitor Lizard</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Asian Water Monitor is one of the largest and most impressive reptiles found in Khao Sok National Park. These powerful lizards can grow to more than two metres in length. They are strong swimmers and are often seen moving through rivers, ponds and wetland areas in search of food.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although they may appear intimidating, Asian Water Monitors generally avoid people. They spend much of their time hunting fish, crabs, insects and other small animals. Visitors are often surprised by how quietly they move through the water despite their size.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Asian Water Monitor is one of the reptiles guests are most likely to encounter during a stay in Khao Sok. Sightings around rivers and streams are relatively common, particularly during the warmer hours of the day.
        </p>
