        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Tokay Gecko</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Tokay Gecko is one of the most recognisable reptiles found in Khao Sok. With its striking grey-blue body covered in bright orange or red spots, it is also one of the most colourful gecko species in Thailand.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Tokay Geckos are nocturnal and spend their days hidden in tree hollows, roof spaces and other sheltered locations. After dark they emerge to hunt insects, spiders and other small prey. They are best known for their distinctive call, which sounds remarkably like the words "to-kay", giving the species its common name.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although often heard before they are seen, Tokay Geckos are relatively common around buildings and forest edges. Visitors staying in Khao Sok may hear their loud calls shortly after sunset or spot them clinging to walls and tree trunks after dark.
        </p>
