        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Barred Flying Dragon</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Barred Flying Dragon is one of the most unusual reptiles found in Khao Sok National Park. Despite its name, it is not a dragon but a small lizard capable of gliding between trees using wing-like membranes that extend from its ribs.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These remarkable reptiles spend most of their lives in the forest canopy, where they feed on ants and other small insects. Their mottled brown colouring provides excellent camouflage against tree bark, making them surprisingly difficult to spot when stationary.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although they cannot truly fly, Barred Flying Dragons can glide impressive distances from tree to tree in search of food or to escape predators. Lucky visitors occasionally encounter them around Riverside Cottages and during jungle hikes through the rainforest.
        </p>
