        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Mangrove Cat Snake</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Mangrove Cat Snake is one of the most striking snakes found in the Khao Sok rainforest. Its distinctive black body marked with bright yellow bands makes it one of the easiest snakes to recognise, particularly during night-time wildlife encounters.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          A skilled climber, the Mangrove Cat Snake spends much of its time in trees and dense vegetation, where it hunts lizards, frogs and other small animals. Like many rainforest snakes, it is primarily active after dark and relies on excellent camouflage and stealth to approach its prey.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One of the best places to spot a Mangrove Cat Snake is on a <a href="/khao-sok-canoe-trip-sabai-sabai/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">canoe trip</a>, where they are sometimes seen resting in overhanging branches above the river. Drifting quietly beneath the rainforest canopy offers an excellent opportunity to observe wildlife that might otherwise go unnoticed.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          For many wildlife enthusiasts, seeing one of these beautifully patterned snakes is a memorable part of the Khao Sok rainforest experience.
        </p>
