        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Reticulated Python</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Reticulated Python is the longest snake species in the world and one of the most impressive reptiles found in Khao Sok National Park. These powerful constrictors are non-venomous and subdue their prey by wrapping their bodies around it before swallowing it whole.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite their size, Reticulated Pythons are surprisingly difficult to spot in the rainforest. Their patterned scales provide excellent camouflage among leaves, roots and branches, allowing them to remain almost invisible while waiting for prey to approach.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although sightings are uncommon, Reticulated Pythons are occasionally encountered during wildlife activities in Khao Sok. Finding one resting in a tree or stretched out beside the river is a memorable experience for many visitors.
        </p>
