        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Golden Tree Frog</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Golden Tree Frog is one of the most commonly encountered amphibians in the Khao Sok rainforest. These colourful little frogs are often found near streams, ponds and other wet areas, where their sticky toe pads allow them to climb effortlessly through vegetation and even cling to smooth leaves and branches.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Most active after dark, Golden Tree Frogs emerge to hunt insects, spiders and other small prey. Their calls are a familiar sound on warm tropical evenings, particularly during the rainy season when amphibian activity increases dramatically.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Visitors staying at Riverside Cottages or exploring the rainforest after sunset have a good chance of encountering these attractive frogs. Their bright colours and large eyes make them a favourite subject for wildlife photographers.
        </p>
