        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Kuhl's Flying Gecko</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Kuhl's Flying Gecko, also known as the Gliding Gecko, is one of the most remarkable reptiles found in the Khao Sok rainforest. Its flattened body, fringed skin and intricate camouflage help it blend almost perfectly into tree bark, making it extremely difficult to spot during the day.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite its name, the Kuhl's Flying Gecko does not truly fly. Instead, it can glide between trees using flaps of skin along its body and tail. This unusual adaptation helps it escape predators and move through the forest canopy.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although well camouflaged, visitors occasionally encounter Kuhl's Flying Geckos during night walks and wildlife tours. Their unusual appearance makes them one of the most fascinating reptiles in the rainforest.
