        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>KHAO SOK JUNGLE BIRDS</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is one of Thailand's most rewarding destinations for birdwatching, with hundreds of bird species recorded within its ancient rainforest. From colourful kingfishers and broadbills to majestic hornbills and birds of prey, the park supports an extraordinary variety of birdlife throughout the year.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Many species can be seen around Riverside Cottages, while others are more often encountered during lake tours, jungle hikes and dedicated birdwatching excursions. Early morning is generally the best time for birdwatching, when the rainforest comes alive with birdsong and activity.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Visitors with a particular interest in birds can also join one of our guided birdwatching tours, led by experienced local guides familiar with the calls, behaviour and habitats of Khao Sok's remarkable birdlife.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Great Hornbill</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Great Hornbill is one of the most spectacular birds found in Khao Sok National Park. Easily recognised by its enormous yellow bill and distinctive casque, this impressive bird is often seen flying above the rainforest canopy or feeding in fruiting trees.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Figs are an important part of the Great Hornbill's diet, making these birds valuable seed dispersers that help maintain the health of the rainforest. They are usually seen in pairs or small family groups and are among the most sought-after bird sightings in Khao Sok.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One of the most remarkable features of the Great Hornbill is its nesting behaviour. The female seals herself inside a tree cavity while raising her young, relying on the male to bring food throughout the nesting period.
        </p>
