        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Crested Serpent Eagle</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Crested Serpent Eagle is one of the most impressive birds of prey found in Khao Sok National Park. Often seen soaring above the rainforest canopy, this distinctive eagle can be recognised by its broad wings, short crest and piercing yellow eyes.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          As its name suggests, snakes form an important part of the Crested Serpent Eagle's diet, although it also feeds on lizards, frogs and other small animals. Its excellent eyesight allows it to spot prey from high above the forest before swooping down to make a capture.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Visitors often hear the eagle's distinctive whistling call before they spot it circling overhead. Sightings are most common in open areas, along rivers and above the forest canopy, where these magnificent birds take advantage of rising warm air currents.
        </p>
