        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Brown Wood Owl</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Brown Wood Owl is one of the most mysterious birds found in the Khao Sok rainforest. Active mainly after dark, these large owls spend their days resting quietly in the forest before emerging at dusk to hunt.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          With their large dark eyes, powerful talons and silent flight, Brown Wood Owls are highly effective predators. They feed on a variety of small animals, including rodents, reptiles and insects, using their excellent hearing and eyesight to locate prey in the darkness.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Visitors are more likely to hear a Brown Wood Owl than see one. Their distinctive calls often echo through the rainforest after sunset, creating one of the most memorable sounds of a night in Khao Sok. A resident pair is occasionally seen around Riverside Cottages, while sightings are also possible during guided nighttime wildlife activities.
        </p>
