        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Black-and-red Broadbill</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Black-and-red Broadbill is one of the most colourful birds found in Khao Sok National Park. With its bright red body, black head and striking blue bill, it is a favourite among birdwatchers and wildlife photographers visiting the rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These distinctive birds are often found near rivers and streams, where they search for insects, small frogs and other prey among the vegetation. Broadbills are also known for their remarkable hanging nests, which are woven from plant fibres and suspended from branches above water.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although they can be difficult to spot among the dense foliage, Black-and-red Broadbills are regularly encountered in suitable habitat around Khao Sok. Their vivid colours make them one of the most rewarding bird sightings for visitors exploring the rainforest.
        </p>
