        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Blue-winged pitta</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Blue-winged Pitta is one of the most colourful and sought-after birds found in Khao Sok National Park. With its striking blue wings, buff-coloured body and contrasting black-and-white head markings, this beautiful bird is a favourite among birdwatchers visiting the rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Unlike many birds that spend their time high in the canopy, Blue-winged Pittas are often found on or near the forest floor. They search through leaf litter and vegetation for insects, worms and other small prey, usually close to streams and damp areas of the rainforest.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although they can be surprisingly difficult to spot, their bright colours make them unmistakable when seen. Patient observers may encounter Blue-winged Pittas around Riverside Cottages or during guided hikes through suitable forest habitat.
        </p>
