        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Kingfishers</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is home to more than a dozen species of kingfisher, making it one of the best places in Thailand to observe these colourful birds. While many people associate kingfishers with brilliant blue plumage, some species found in Khao Sok, such as the Ruddy Kingfisher, display rich chestnut-red colouring.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Kingfishers are most often seen perched quietly above rivers and streams, watching for fish, frogs, insects and freshwater crabs. Their rapid dives and remarkable hunting skills make them fascinating birds to observe.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One of the most remarkable features of a kingfisher is its colour. The brilliant blue feathers seen on many species are not produced by blue pigment. Instead, the microscopic structure of the feathers reflects blue light, creating their striking appearance.
        </p>
