        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Grey-breasted spiderhunter</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Grey-breasted Spiderhunter is one of the more unusual birds found in the Khao Sok rainforest. With its olive-green plumage and long curved bill, it is specially adapted for feeding on nectar from flowers, particularly those of banana plants, gingers and other tropical species.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although its name suggests a diet of spiders, the Grey-breasted Spiderhunter feeds on a variety of insects as well as nectar. It is most often seen alone or in pairs, moving quietly through the lower levels of the rainforest in search of food.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Patient observers may spot Grey-breasted Spiderhunters around flowering plants and forest edges, where their distinctive shape and feeding behaviour make them easier to identify than many other rainforest birds.
        </p>
