        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>INSECTS & ARACHNIDS</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          While larger animals often attract the most attention, many of the Khao Sok rainforest's most remarkable creatures are found among its insects and arachnids. From giant Atlas Moths and colourful Lantern Bugs to intricate orb-weaver spiders and perfectly camouflaged praying mantises, these smaller inhabitants play an essential role in the rainforest ecosystem.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Many species are most active after dark, making night walks an excellent opportunity to discover a hidden world that many visitors rarely notice. For wildlife photographers, insects and arachnids often provide some of the most fascinating and rewarding subjects in the rainforest.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Atlas Moth</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Atlas Moth is one of the largest moths in the world and one of the most remarkable insects found in the Khao Sok rainforest. With a wingspan that can exceed 25 centimetres, encountering one at night is an unforgettable experience.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite its impressive size, the adult Atlas Moth lives for only a short time. In fact, it cannot eat at all. After emerging from its cocoon, the moth survives entirely on energy stored during its caterpillar stage, spending its brief adult life searching for a mate before its life cycle comes to an end.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Atlas Moths are most often seen after dark and are a favourite sighting on night walks through the rainforest.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
