        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Golden Orb Weaver Spider</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Golden Orb Weaver Spider is one of the most impressive arachnids found in the Khao Sok rainforest. Although the spider itself is striking, it is best known for the enormous golden-coloured webs it creates between trees and shrubs.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Female Golden Orb Weavers are much larger than the males and can reach impressive sizes when their legs are included. Their webs may span several metres and shimmer with a distinctive golden colour when illuminated by sunlight.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite their intimidating appearance, Golden Orb Weavers are harmless to people. They play an important role in controlling insect populations within the rainforest. Their spectacular webs are often among the first things visitors notice while exploring jungle trails.
        </p>
