        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Lantern Bug</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Lantern Bug is one of the most unusual insects found in the Khao Sok rainforest. With its striking colours and distinctive elongated head, it often looks more like a creature from a fantasy film than a real rainforest insect.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Despite its name, the Lantern Bug does not produce light. Early naturalists mistakenly believed the insect's unusual head structure functioned as a lantern, giving rise to its common name. Today, it remains one of the most distinctive insects found in Southeast Asia.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Lantern Bugs feed primarily on plant sap and are usually found resting on tree trunks and branches during the day. Their remarkable appearance makes them a favourite subject for wildlife photographers and nature enthusiasts exploring the rainforest.
        </p>
