        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Best Viewing Opportunities:</strong> Riverside Cottages | <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Jungle Hikes</a> | <a href="/khao-sok-trekking-hiking/#night" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Night Safari</a>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Cicada</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The Cicada is responsible for one of the most distinctive sounds of the Khao Sok rainforest. On warm days, the loud buzzing and humming calls of male cicadas can fill the forest, creating the soundtrack that many visitors associate with the tropics.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although adult cicadas are easy to hear, they are often surprisingly difficult to spot. Most of their lives are spent underground as nymphs, emerging only when they are ready to transform into winged adults. Depending on the species, this underground stage can last for several years.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Once they emerge, adult cicadas live only a short time, focused on finding a mate and continuing the cycle. Their brief appearance may be short-lived, but their calls are among the most memorable sounds of the rainforest.
        </p>
