        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Bamboo</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Bamboo is one of the most recognisable plants in the Khao Sok rainforest. Dense bamboo thickets are found throughout the forest and provide food and shelter for a wide variety of wildlife.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Although often mistaken for a tree, bamboo is actually a giant grass. It is also one of the fastest-growing plants on Earth, with some species capable of growing almost a metre in a single day. Despite its lightweight appearance, bamboo is remarkably strong and has a tensile strength comparable to steel.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Bamboo plays an important role in the rainforest ecosystem. It helps stabilise soil, creates habitat for countless insects and animals, and provides food for species including elephants and bamboo rats. Along many <a href="/khao-sok-jungle-hike/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">jungle trails</a>, towering stands of bamboo are among the most distinctive features of the Khao Sok landscape.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/bamboo.jpg"
            alt="Bamboo - khao national park"
