        </figure>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Liana</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Lianas are the woody climbing vines that twist, climb and drape through the Khao Sok rainforest. Rather than supporting themselves like trees, they use surrounding vegetation to reach sunlight high in the forest canopy.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These remarkable plants can grow to enormous lengths, linking trees together and creating natural pathways through the forest. Many animals, including monkeys, squirrels and insects, use lianas to move through the canopy without descending to the ground.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Lianas are an important part of the rainforest ecosystem, providing food, shelter and travel routes for wildlife. Their tangled stems and hanging vines are among the most distinctive features of the Khao Sok jungle and help create the dense, layered appearance of the rainforest.
        </p>
